{"type":"text","text":"The redesign addresses the core layout: pale slate background, navy header at (48,48) sized 1184×120, three equal cards in one row with 24px gaps starting at y=200, and the footer visible within the viewport with no overflow. Now I'll refine spacing/typography as the most notable remaining category. The main issue is the large empty gap: about 240px of dead space sits between the cards and the footer, and the cards have a weak visual hierarchy because the caption is pinned to the bottom far from the value, leaving a big void inside each card. I'll pull the card text together, add a little breathing room around the value, and size the footer block to sit closer below the cards instead of being pushed to the viewport bottom."}
